 * Compression is expanded on re-emit, so forwarded responses grow. The client
   query is read into a 512-byte buffer and replies are sent with no EDNS
   handling and no truncation (TC) bit. A response that grows past 512 (or past
   the client's advertised size) can break non-EDNS clients. Consider honoring
   the query's EDNS payload size and setting TC when over the limit.
 * The Eq/Hash of DnsDomainName should depend on lower case string of domain.
 * dnscrypt-proxy reply with notes AAAA is disabled.
 * DohResolvCache never refreshed
